<BaseLayout title="Sources and corrections" description="How RentSmart Home checks products, tenancy information and correction requests.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="section-kicker">Check the details</p><h1>Sources &amp; corrections.</h1><p>Product instructions, tenancy documents and local rules matter more than a generic promise that something is “renter-friendly.”</p></div></section>
<section class="container content-section"><div class="prose">
<h2>Preferred sources</h2><ul><li>Manufacturer instructions for installation, load ratings, compatible surfaces and removal.</li><li>Official government or regulator guidance for tenancy, deposit, building and safety rules.</li><li>Recognised legal-aid resources for jurisdiction-specific explanations.</li><li>Direct price checks and receipts where an article reports actual project costs.</li></ul>
<h2>Read product claims carefully</h2><p>Check the exact model, surface type, load direction, application conditions, curing time and removal instructions. A test on one wall does not prove the same result on old paint, wallpaper, damp plaster or a different finish.</p>
<h2>Request a correction</h2><p>Use the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a> to send the article URL, exact statement, product model or location, and supporting evidence. We assess requests on their merits and may correct, clarify, update or explain why a claim remains unchanged.</p>
<h2>Tenancy information</h2><p>The <a href="/tenancy-rules/us/">US renter guide</a> and <a href="/tenancy-rules/uk/">England renter guide</a> link to official starting points; neither replaces checking the current rule and your own tenancy agreement.</p>
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
